# Cursor AI Rules — Shokitora Project Governance
# ===================================================

# 1. Project Memory & Ledger
- This repository uses Shokitora (SQLite ledger) for engineering tracking.
- Query active tasks before starting work: `shoki task:list`
- Query architectural decisions before refactoring: `shoki list --category decision --limit 5`
- Query past learnings before debugging complex issues: `shoki list --category learning --limit 5`

# 2. Strict Zero Plaintext Secrets Policy
- NEVER generate, edit, or commit plaintext `.env` files.
- NEVER hardcode API keys (ghp_, sk-, etc.) into source code.
- Always use Shokitora Sovereign Vault for secrets:
  - `shoki vault set <key> <value> --expires-in 90d`
  - `shoki vault run -- <command>`
  - `shoki vault triage [service]`

# 3. Post-Task Completion
- When completing a task:
  - Mark completed: `shoki update <task_id> --status COMPLETED --hours <hours>`
  - If a design choice was made: `shoki add decision "<why>" --parent <task_id>`
  - If an issue was resolved: `shoki add learning "<how>" --parent <task_id>`
